## 4. ARCHITECTURE DECISIONS (LOCKED — Chat #78)

### Transport layer
**n8n webhook** (not Express.js — production RDA pipeline already uses n8n, infrastructure is stable, zero new setup).

### Claude calls
**Full 5-call RDA architecture** — NOT a single call.

**Why:** Single call produces generic output. Generic output = no signup. Quality IS the demo. The 5-call chain is what produces non-generic, precise drafts. Accept 10-15 second latency. Show a progress indicator.

### Latency handling
Progress indicator with 4 stages shown to user:
```
"Analyzing review signal..."     (~3 sec)
"Calibrating brand voice..."     (~3 sec)
"Drafting response..."           (~3 sec)
"Running quality audit..."       (~3 sec)
```

### Input source
User provides directly on landing page:
- Review text (300-500 characters)
- Brand voice preferences (tone, vocabulary, formality, phrases to avoid)
- Restaurant name + location (for SEO signature)

**No NocoDB Client Config lookup required** — user provides brand voice inline in the demo form.

### Output
Public response draft only (no internal brief shown to demo user).

### Logging
Every demo request logged to NocoDB demo table: review text + brand voice input + generated draft + timestamp + session ID.

### Abuse prevention
IP-based rate limit: max 3 demo requests per IP per hour.

### Governance
Same governance constraints as production RDA apply:
- No refund/voucher/discount language
- No email addresses or URLs in draft
- No placeholder text
- No "We apologize for any inconvenience"

